// Title: Webshell Tool Reconnaissance Activity
// ID: f64e5c19-879c-4bae-b471-6d84c8339677
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Cian Heasley, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2020-07-22
// Tags: attack.persistence, attack.t1505.003
// Description: Detects processes spawned from web servers (PHP, Tomcat, IIS, etc.) that perform reconnaissance looking for the existence of popular scripting tools (perl, python, wget) on the system via the help commands
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where ((((process.parent.executable endswith "\\java.exe" or process.parent.executable endswith "\\javaw.exe") and (process.parent.executable like "*_-tomcat-*" or process.parent.executable like "*_\\tomcat*")) or ((process.parent.executable endswith "\\java.exe" or process.parent.executable endswith "\\javaw.exe") and (process.command_line like "*_CATALINA_HOME*" or process.command_line like "*_catalina.jar*")) or ((process.parent.executable endswith "\\caddy.exe" or process.parent.executable endswith "\\httpd.exe" or process.parent.executable endswith "\\nginx.exe" or process.parent.executable endswith "\\php-cgi.exe" or process.parent.executable endswith "\\w3wp.exe" or process.parent.executable endswith "\\ws_tomcatservice.exe"))) and ((process.command_line like "*_perl --help*" or process.command_line like "*_perl -h*" or process.command_line like "*_python --help*" or process.command_line like "*_python -h*" or process.command_line like "*_python3 --help*" or process.command_line like "*_python3 -h*" or process.command_line like "*_wget --help*")))
